diff --git a/docs/storage-usage.md b/docs/storage-usage.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..def7220
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/storage-usage.md
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+# Storage usage
+
+`Account#bytes_used` and `Board#bytes_used` read the latest background-calculated
+byte total. Empty accounts and boards return zero. Reads do not load attachments
+or cache the value on the model instance.
+
+We count each attachment's blob size for card images and Action Text embeds in
+board public descriptions, card descriptions, and comment bodies. A blob attached
+in two places counts in both places. Avatars, exports/imports, unattached direct
+uploads, previews, and variants do not count. Draft and closed cards count too.
+
+## Refreshing totals
+
+The `reconcile_storage_usage` recurring task dispatches work every minute. Run the
+Solid Queue worker with recurring tasks enabled. Changes become visible after the
+next dispatch and completion of the background jobs; these are eventually
+consistent totals, not synchronous quota enforcement.
+
+Attachment additions and removals write a durable ledger entry in the same
+transaction as the attachment. Moves mark the card's entries (including comments)
+dirty. Multiple changes coalesce into one pending entry. We retain the previously
+accounted board and size so deletions and moves can subtract the correct usage
+even after their source records or blobs are gone.
+
+Each job processes at most 100 entries, resolves current board membership in bulk,
+and applies grouped deltas. The ledger and totals commit together. An account's
+separate total row serializes its aggregation jobs, so concurrent or retried jobs
+cannot apply a delta twice. User edits never lock that shared total row. Dirty
+entries remain available to the next dispatcher if a job is interrupted or an
+enqueue fails. No full-board or full-account attachment scan is needed for normal
+updates.
+
+## Existing data and imports
+
+After deploying the migration, enqueue the initial backfill:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails storage:backfill
+```
+
+Backfill scans attachments in bounded, resumable background batches and is safe to
+repeat while people use the application. Completed account imports automatically
+enqueue their own backfill because imports bypass model callbacks. Derived ledger
+entries and totals are not included in account exports.
+
+As with other callback-maintained data, raw SQL or `delete_all` on source models
+bypasses tracking. Use the normal attachment and model APIs (including detach,
+purge, and purge_later) for changes to counted attachments.
